PART 3 -- g_0i SECTOR: linearized momentum constraint for a moving source (sympy, no quoted formula)
======================================================================================================
  [ok] 3.1 sympy linearized-G routine: G^(1)[pure gauge] = 0 identically (all 16 components)
  [ok] 3.2 EXACT identity G^(1)_{0i} = sigma * d_j(K^j_i - delta K) for arbitrary amplitudes
         sigma = 1; also verifies G^(1)_{0i} contains NO h_00 term (h_00-coefficient: 0, 0)
  [ok] 3.2b the 0i equation is independent of the lapse potential h_00 (pure momentum sector)
  [ok] 3.3a dust source: T_{0i} = -rho w_i at leading order (index lowering, sympy)
  [ok] 3.3b GR anchor: transverse h_0x = -4 V_x  (= the known PPN -(7/2)V-(1/2)W transverse part)
         h_0x = -16*pi*G*rho*w_x/k**2
  [ok] 3.3c GR longitudinal 0i-equation: no h_0z dependence and identically satisfied (continuity) -- longitudinal h_0i is GAUGE in GR, as it must be
  [ok] 3.4a MMG 0i system + trace-Ktilde = 0: unique solution for (h_0i, mu_3)
  [info] 3.4b MMG solution   h_0x = -16*pi*G*rho*w_x/k**2,   h_0z = -12*pi*G*rho*w_z/k**2,   mu_3 = -8*I*pi*G*rho*w_z/k**3
  [ok] 3.4c MMG h_0i matches the PPN (V_i, W_i) structure exactly
  [ok] 3.4d g_0i = -(7/2) V_i - (1/2) W_i  -- numerically GR's PPN-gauge form, but with gamma = 0 the PPN dictionary reads it very differently
         c_V = -7/2, c_W = -1/2

======================================================================================================
PART 4 -- THE PPN DICTIONARY SOLVE AND THE BOUNDS TABLE
======================================================================================================
  [ok] 4.1 the PPN dictionary has a unique solution (xi undetermined by point-dust probes)

   ===========================  PPN PARAMETERS OF MMG_constraint_first  ===========================
   gamma_PPN = 0                (GR 1;  Cassini |gamma-1| < 2.3e-5)
   beta_PPN  = 1                (GR 1;  LLR/Mercury |beta-1| < ~1e-4)
   alpha_1   = 4                (bound |alpha_1| < 1e-4)
   alpha_2   = 0                (bound |alpha_2| < ~2e-7 .. 2e-9)
   alpha_3   = -1               (bound |alpha_3| < 4e-20; also = momentum non-conservation)
   zeta_1 = 2*xi,  zeta_2 = 1 - xi,  zeta_3 = 0,  zeta_4 = 2*xi/3   (xi not probed here)
   ================================================================================================
  [ok] 4.2 alpha_1 = 4  ->  violates the |alpha_1| < 1e-4 bound by 4.0e4 x
         physical origin: gamma = 0 removes the 4*gamma part of the V_i coefficient; the gravito-magnetic sector is GR-like, so the mismatch is booked entirely as alpha_1
  [ok] 4.3 alpha_2 = 0  ->  PASSES the solar-spin-axis bound (the one clean pass)
  [ok] 4.4 alpha_3 = -1  ->  violates the pulsar bound |alpha_3| < 4e-20 by 2.5e19 x
         physical origin: the lapse responds INSTANTANEOUSLY (elliptic C_M) to the source's kinetic energy with coefficient 1 instead of GR's retardation-consistent 4; alpha_3 != 0 also means the theory is non-conservative (self-accelerating binaries)
  [info] 4.5 Mercury perihelion   (2+2g-b)/3 = 0.3333 -> 14.33 arcsec/cy vs observed 42.98+-0.04 => 716 sigma
  [ok] 4.5 perihelion: excluded at > 500 sigma

  THEORY-SPECIFIC PREFERRED-FRAME TERMS (beyond the alpha's):
   (i)   alpha_3 = -1: the elliptic (action-at-a-distance) lapse response.  In a frame moving at
         w relative to the foliation this generates the PPN term -(alpha_1-alpha_2-alpha_3) w^2 U
         = -(5) w^2 U in g_00 and (2 alpha_3 - alpha_1) w^i V_i = -6 w^i V_i; with w ~ 369 km/s
         (CMB frame) these are ~7.6e-6 U effects -- 2 orders above the Cassini gamma precision,
         5 above pulsar timing sensitivity to alpha_3.
   (ii)  the k = 0 scalar zero-mode pair (q, p) survives S_2, S_3 and is 'reserved for cosmology'
         (Gate 7): the preferred foliation has an undetermined homogeneous mode -- no PPN effect,
         but the PPN frame itself is only defined up to it.
   (iii) the a0-scale EFE quadrupole (PART 5): kernel-dependent, aligned with the GALACTIC-CENTRE
         direction (not the CMB dipole) -- separable from (i) by axis, per the corpus's audit3.

